-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat notified from part P0 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P0-seat-notified: the seat questions of Articles 1 to 4, 111 and 113 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744), asked by a notified body: a conformity assessment body notified in accordance with the Regulation and other relevant Union harmonisation legislation (Article 3(22)).
--
-- LAYER 2 (the seat layer). Every question below calls a function of the keel (aia-scope, aia-definitions, aia-literacy, aia-timeline, aia-annex-x) and restates no rule.
-- The keel decides what the text means, the date it applies from and which text is in force; this file asks, in the words and with the facts of this seat, what a person in the seat can state.
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it. The role facts are asked once, in the question under Article 3 (or Article 2 for a product manufacturer and a person affected),
-- and no other question asks them again; where a keel function needs the role as a fact, this file passes TRUE.
--
-- THE DATE ASKED. Every question whose answer depends on a date asks `the date asked`. It selects the text in force (the Regulation as enacted until 26 July 2026, as amended from 27 July 2026,
-- the day the Omnibus enters into force) and whether the provision applies yet (Chapter I from 2 February 2025; the group General from 2 August 2026).
-- The other shared inputs (the placement date, the significant-change flag, the route by which the AI system is high-risk) carry the same name and @desc in every question that needs them.
--
-- RESULTS. A MAYBE BOOLEAN or MAYBE DATE answer of NOTHING means "not covered": the provision does not speak to these facts, or has not begun to apply, or is not in the text in force on the date asked.
-- JUST FALSE is the text's own "no" (a flat negative such as "does not apply", or a condition it states). The answer of a keel function is passed through unchanged; nothing here turns NOTHING into FALSE.
-- An exported obligation (a DEONTIC answer) is shown by a form as the placeholder "<obligation>"; its content is read with #TRACE in the case file.
--
-- STATUS. Commencement is IN for this Regulation (assumed, not ruled). The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect (it says so itself, line 2 of the file).
-- The readings are the keel's (NOTES.md, fork register) and this layer's (NOTES.md, fork register P0): assumed, not ruled by a lawyer.
-- The Interact form and jl4-service were not run; l4 check, l4 run and l4 batch were.

§ `Article 1: does Chapter I apply on the date asked?`
-- Chapter I (Articles 1 to 4a) applies from 2 February 2025 (Art 113 third paragraph, point (a)).
-- Article 1 itself creates no rule (a purpose clause and a statement of contents): the one question a seat asks of it is whether the Chapter it opens applies.

-- src:1656 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:1660 | (a) Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025, with the exception of Article 5(1), first subparagraph, points (ba) and (bb), and Article 5(1a) and (1b) which shall apply from 2 December 2026;
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2202 | Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025;
@ref Art 113 first paragraph and third paragraph point (a): Chapter I (src:1656) (src:1660) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2202)
-- The question is asked of no AI system, so the core's two constants stand in for the route and the placement date, and the design is not changed (FALSE).
@export Under Article 1, as a notified body, does Chapter I apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 1, as a notified body, does Chapter I apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter I` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)


§ `Article 3(3) to (8): does the definition of my role fit me?`
-- The role question of the seat: the other questions of this file assume the answer is yes.

-- src:73 | (8) ‘operator’ means a provider, product manufacturer, deployer, authorised representative, importer or distributor;
@ref Art 3(8) (src:73)
-- No fact is asked: the seat fixes the role passed to the keel (a person who holds another role asks that seat's question).
@export Under Article 3(8), as a notified body, am I an operator?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(8), as a notified body, am I an operator` IS
    `Art 3(8) the role is an operator` `Notified body`


§ `Article 3(21), (22): am I a notified body?`
-- The role question of the notified body seat.

-- src:91 | (21) ‘conformity assessment body’ means a body that performs third-party conformity assessment activities, including testing, certification and inspection;
-- src:92 | (22) ‘notified body’ means a conformity assessment body notified in accordance with this Regulation and other relevant Union harmonisation legislation;
@ref Art 3(21) and Art 3(22) (src:91-92)
-- The conformity assessment body of Article 3(21) is worked out from the first fact.
@export Under Article 3(22), as a notified body, does the definition of a notified body fit me?
GIVEN `I perform third-party conformity assessment activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you perform third-party conformity assessment activities, including testing, certification and inspection?
      `I am notified in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you notified in accordance with this Regulation?
      `I am notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation? Answer yes if no other such legislation is relevant.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(22), as a notified body, does the definition of a notified body fit me` IS
    `Art 3(22) the body is a notified body` (`Art 3(21) the body is a conformity assessment body` `I perform third-party conformity assessment activities`) `I am notified in accordance with this Regulation` `I am notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant`


§ `Article 3(23): substantial modification`
-- Only if a change has been made to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service.

-- src:93 | (23) ‘substantial modification’ means a change to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service which is not foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider and as a result of which the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected or results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed;
@ref Art 3(23) (src:93)
@export Under Article 3(23), as a notified body, is the change a substantial modification?
GIVEN `the change is to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the change made to the AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service?
      `the change is foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the change foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider?
      `as a result of the change the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As a result of the change, is the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 affected?
      `the change results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the change result in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 3(23), as a notified body, is the change a substantial modification` IS
    `Art 3(23) the change is a substantial modification` `the change is to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service` `the change is foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider` `as a result of the change the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected` `the change results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed`


§ `Article 111 and Article 113: does the group General apply on the date asked?`
-- The group General holds every provision that no point of Article 113 dates separately, among them Articles 111 to 113 themselves: it applies from 2 August 2026 (Art 113, second paragraph).
-- The question is asked of no AI system, so the core's two constants stand in for the route and the placement date, and the design is not changed (FALSE).

-- src:1656 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:1657 | It shall apply from 2 August 2026.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2198 | This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2199 | It shall apply from 2 August 2026.
@ref Art 113 first and second paragraphs: the group General (Articles 111 to 113 and every provision no point of Article 113 dates) (src:1656-1657) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:2198-2199)
-- A legacy high-risk AI system saved by Article 111(2) is a separate question (Under Article 111(2), first sentence).
@export Under Article 111, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 111, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` General `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat notified from part P2 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P2-seat-notified.l4: the seat of a notified body, over the layer-1 modules of part P2 (Article 4a, Articles 8 to 15, Annex IV).
-- It calls the layer-1 rules and never restates one. Every question has @export and @desc and takes plain inputs; the records a rule expects are built in a WHERE.
-- The shared inputs have the same names and @desc in every question: the date asked; the route by which the AI system is high-risk; the date it was placed on the market or put into service; whether its design was significantly changed since Chapter III applied.
-- A result of NOTHING is "not covered" (not yet applicable, saved by Article 111(2), or outside what the text says); JUST FALSE is the text's own "no".
-- The seat assumes its role: the person asking holds it (the role question below calls the keel's definition once).

§ `The role and the applicability of the provisions`

@export Under Article 11, as a notified body, am I a notified body within the meaning of Article 3(22)?
GIVEN `the body is a conformity assessment body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your body perform third-party conformity assessment activities, including testing, certification and inspection?
      `it is notified in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your body been notified in accordance with this Regulation?
      `it is notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your body been notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation? Answer yes if no other such legislation is relevant.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 11, as a notified body, am I a notified body within the meaning of Article 3(22)` IS
    JUST (`Art 3(22) the body is a notified body` `the body is a conformity assessment body` `it is notified in accordance with this Regulation` `it is notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant`)

@export Under Article 8, as a notified body, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 8, as a notified body, does Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Chapter III Sections 1 to 3` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)


§ `Under Annex IV: the technical documentation`

@export Under Annex IV point 1, as a notified body, does the technical documentation I was given contain a general description of the AI system including the eight items the point lists?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation this question is about? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the application of the requirement or obligation this question is about leave the overall level of protection provided by this Regulation undiminished? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the technical documentation contains a general description of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains a general description of the AI system?
      `the technical documentation contains its intended purpose, the name of the provider and the version of the system reflecting its relation to previous versions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains its intended purpose, the name of the provider and the version of the system reflecting its relation to previous versions?
      `the technical documentation contains how the AI system interacts with, or can be used to interact with, hardware or software, including with other AI systems, that are not part of the AI system itself, where applicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the technical documentation contain how the AI system interacts with, or can be used to interact with, hardware or software, including with other AI systems, that are not part of the AI system itself, where that is applicable? Answer yes if it is not applicable.
      `the technical documentation contains the versions of relevant software or firmware, and any requirements related to version updates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the versions of relevant software or firmware, and any requirements related to version updates?
      `the technical documentation contains the description of all the forms in which the AI system is placed on the market or put into service, such as software packages embedded into hardware, downloads, or APIs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the description of all the forms in which the AI system is placed on the market or put into service, such as software packages embedded into hardware, downloads, or APIs?
      `the technical documentation contains the description of the hardware on which the AI system is intended to run` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the description of the hardware on which the AI system is intended to run?
      `the technical documentation contains where the AI system is a component of products, photographs or illustrations showing external features, the marking and internal layout of those products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the technical documentation contain where the AI system is a component of products, photographs or illustrations showing external features, the marking and internal layout of those products? Answer yes if it is not a component of products.
      `the technical documentation contains a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer?
      `the technical documentation contains instructions for use for the deployer, and a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer, where applicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the technical documentation contain instructions for use for the deployer, and a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer, where that is applicable? Answer yes if it is not applicable.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Annex IV point 1, as a notified body, does the technical documentation I was given contain a general description of the AI system including the eight items the point lists` IS
    `Annex IV point 1 the technical documentation contains a general description of the AI system` `the date asked` `the AI system as stated` `the harmonisation facts as stated` `the technical documentation contains a general description of the AI system` `the technical documentation contains its intended purpose, the name of the provider and the version of the system reflecting its relation to previous versions` `the technical documentation contains how the AI system interacts with, or can be used to interact with, hardware or software, including with other AI systems, that are not part of the AI system itself, where applicable` `the technical documentation contains the versions of relevant software or firmware, and any requirements related to version updates` `the technical documentation contains the description of all the forms in which the AI system is placed on the market or put into service, such as software packages embedded into hardware, downloads, or APIs` `the technical documentation contains the description of the hardware on which the AI system is intended to run` `the technical documentation contains where the AI system is a component of products, photographs or illustrations showing external features, the marking and internal layout of those products` `the technical documentation contains a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer` `the technical documentation contains instructions for use for the deployer, and a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer, where applicable`
    WHERE
        `the AI system as stated` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the harmonisation facts as stated` MEANS `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts` WITH
            `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`
            `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

@export Under Annex IV point 2, as a notified body, does the technical documentation I was given contain a detailed description of the elements of the AI system and of the process for its development, including the eight items the point lists?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lay down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights than the requirement or obligation this question is about? Answer no if you do not know of such legislation.
      `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would limiting the application of the requirement or obligation this question is about leave the overall level of protection provided by this Regulation undiminished? Answer no if you do not know.
      `the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the elements of the AI system and of the process for its development` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the elements of the AI system and of the process for its development?
      `the technical documentation contains the methods and steps performed for the development of the AI system, including, where relevant, recourse to pre-trained systems or tools provided by third parties and how those were used, integrated or modified by the provider` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the technical documentation contain the methods and steps performed for the development of the AI system, including, where relevant, recourse to pre-trained systems or tools provided by third parties and how those were used, integrated or modified by the provider? Answer yes if it is not relevant.
      `the technical documentation contains the design specifications of the system, namely the general logic of the AI system and of the algorithms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the design specifications of the system, namely the general logic of the AI system and of the algorithms?
      `the technical documentation contains the key design choices including the rationale and assumptions made, including with regard to persons or groups of persons in respect of who the system is intended to be used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the key design choices including the rationale and assumptions made, including with regard to persons or groups of persons in respect of who the system is intended to be used?
      `the technical documentation contains the main classification choices` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the main classification choices?
      `the technical documentation contains what the system is designed to optimise for, and the relevance of the different parameters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains what the system is designed to optimise for, and the relevance of the different parameters?
      `the technical documentation contains the description of the expected output and output quality of the system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the description of the expected output and output quality of the system?
      `the technical documentation contains the decisions about any possible trade-off made regarding the technical solutions adopted to comply with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the decisions about any possible trade-off made regarding the technical solutions adopted to comply with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2?
      `the technical documentation contains the description of the system architecture explaining how software components build on or feed into each other and integrate into the overall processing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the description of the system architecture explaining how software components build on or feed into each other and integrate into the overall processing?
      `the technical documentation contains the computational resources used to develop, train, test and validate the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the computational resources used to develop, train, test and validate the AI system?
      `the technical documentation contains where relevant, the data requirements in terms of datasheets describing the training methodologies and techniques and the training data sets used, including a general description of these data sets, information about their provenance, scope and main characteristics; how the data was obtained and selected; labelling procedures (e.g. for supervised learning), data cleaning methodologies (e.g. outliers detection)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the technical documentation contain where relevant, the data requirements in terms of datasheets describing the training methodologies and techniques and the training data sets used, including a general description of these data sets, information about their provenance, scope and main characteristics; how the data was obtained and selected; labelling procedures (e.g. for supervised learning), data cleaning methodologies (e.g. outliers detection)? Answer yes if it is not relevant.
      `the technical documentation contains an assessment of the human oversight measures needed in accordance with Article 14, including an assessment of the technical measures needed to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of AI systems by the deployers, in accordance with Article 13(3), point (d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains an assessment of the human oversight measures needed in accordance with Article 14, including an assessment of the technical measures needed to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of AI systems by the deployers, in accordance with Article 13(3), point (d)?
      `the technical documentation contains where applicable, a detailed description of pre-determined changes to the AI system and its performance, together with all the relevant information related to the technical solutions adopted to ensure continuous compliance of the AI system with the relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the technical documentation contain where applicable, a detailed description of pre-determined changes to the AI system and its performance, together with all the relevant information related to the technical solutions adopted to ensure continuous compliance with the relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2? Answer yes if it is not applicable.
      `the technical documentation contains the validation and testing procedures used, including information about the validation and testing data used and their main characteristics` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the validation and testing procedures used, including information about the validation and testing data used and their main characteristics?
      `the technical documentation contains the metrics used to measure accuracy, robustness and compliance with other relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, as well as potentially discriminatory impacts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains the metrics used to measure accuracy, robustness and compliance with other relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, as well as potentially discriminatory impacts?
      `the technical documentation contains test logs and all test reports dated and signed by the responsible persons, including with regard to pre-determined changes as referred to under point (f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains test logs and all test reports dated and signed by the responsible persons, including with regard to pre-determined changes as referred to under point (f)?
      `the technical documentation contains cybersecurity measures put in place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the technical documentation you have been given, is it the case that the technical documentation contains cybersecurity measures put in place?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Annex IV point 2, as a notified body, does the technical documentation I was given contain a detailed description of the elements of the AI system and of the process for its development, including the eight items the point lists` IS
    `Annex IV point 2 the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the elements of the AI system and of the process for its development` `the date asked` `the AI system as stated` `the harmonisation facts as stated` `the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the elements of the AI system and of the process for its development` `the technical documentation contains the methods and steps performed for the development of the AI system, including, where relevant, recourse to pre-trained systems or tools provided by third parties and how those were used, integrated or modified by the provider` `the technical documentation contains the design specifications of the system, namely the general logic of the AI system and of the algorithms` `the technical documentation contains the key design choices including the rationale and assumptions made, including with regard to persons or groups of persons in respect of who the system is intended to be used` `the technical documentation contains the main classification choices` `the technical documentation contains what the system is designed to optimise for, and the relevance of the different parameters` `the technical documentation contains the description of the expected output and output quality of the system` `the technical documentation contains the decisions about any possible trade-off made regarding the technical solutions adopted to comply with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` `the technical documentation contains the description of the system architecture explaining how software components build on or feed into each other and integrate into the overall processing` `the technical documentation contains the computational resources used to develop, train, test and validate the AI system` `the technical documentation contains where relevant, the data requirements in terms of datasheets describing the training methodologies and techniques and the training data sets used, including a general description of these data sets, information about their provenance, scope and main characteristics; how the data was obtained and selected; labelling procedures (e.g. for supervised learning), data cleaning methodologies (e.g. outliers detection)` `the technical documentation contains an assessment of the human oversight measures needed in accordance with Article 14, including an assessment of the technical measures needed to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of AI systems by the deployers, in accordance with Article 13(3), point (d)` `the technical documentation contains where applicable, a detailed description of pre-determined changes to the AI system and its performance, together with all the relevant information related to the technical solutions adopted to ensure continuous compliance of the AI system with the relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` `the technical documentation contains the validation and testing procedures used, including information about the validation and testing data used and their main characteristics` `the technical documentation contains the metrics used to measure accuracy, robustness and compliance with other relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, as well as potentially discriminatory impacts` `the technical documentation contains test logs and all test reports dated and signed by the responsible persons, including with regard to pre-determined changes as referred to under point (f)` `the technical documentation contains cybersecurity measures put in place`
    WHERE
        `the AI system as stated` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`
        `the harmonisation facts as stated` MEANS `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts` WITH
            `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I`
            `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned` IS `Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I lays down requirements or obligations providing an equivalent or higher level of protection of health, safety or fundamental rights as the requirement or obligation concerned`
            `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation` IS `such limitation does not reduce the overall level of protection provided for by this Regulation`

