-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat notified from part P4 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P4-seat-notified: the seat layer over the layer-1 modules of part P4 (Articles 28 to 39, Annex VII, Annex XIV of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744).
-- SEAT: a notified body, or a conformity assessment body that has applied to become one (a group that arises before notification says so in its heading).
-- Each question below is one layer-1 function asked from this seat: it takes the facts this seat could state, as plain inputs (yes/no, a date, a number, or one of the keel's own choices),
-- each with an @desc, and calls the layer-1 function with them; nothing is restated here. A result of JUST TRUE is a yes, JUST FALSE is the text's no, and NOTHING is "the text does not say"
-- (including "this provision does not yet apply on the date asked, or does not apply to this AI system"): see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (P4)".
-- A question about the Articles of the group `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` asks the date asked only (Annex XIV too); a question about Annex VII also asks the route, the placement date and the
-- change flag, because Article 111(2) can save a high-risk AI system placed on the market earlier and unchanged, and two more facts for Article 2(2): whether the products are covered by the legislation listed in Section B of Annex I,
-- and whether the requirements of the Regulation have been integrated in it. For a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with such products an Annex VII question answers JUST FALSE: Article 2(2) lets only Article 6(1),
-- Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 apply, so Article 43 and Annex VII do not (fork F-S14-reach).
-- Official powers and duties appear only as what they mean to this seat; there is never a seat for a notifying authority or the Commission.

§ `The role`

-- The facts that make this person a notified body, asked once; the other questions do not re-ask them. The keel's own definition does the work.
@export Under Article 29, as a notified body, am I a notified body within the meaning of Article 3(22)?
GIVEN `the body is a conformity assessment body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your body a conformity assessment body, that is, a body that performs third-party conformity assessment activities, including testing, certification and inspection?
      `it is notified in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your body been notified in accordance with this Regulation?
      `it is notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your body been notified in accordance with the other relevant Union harmonisation legislation? Answer yes if no other such legislation is relevant to your body.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 29, as a notified body, am I a notified body within the meaning of Article 3(22)` IS
    JUST (`Art 3(22) the body is a notified body` `the body is a conformity assessment body` `it is notified in accordance with this Regulation` `it is notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant`)

