-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat notified from part P7 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P7-seat-notified: THE SEAT LAYER for a notified body, over the layer-1 modules of Articles 57 to 71 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act
-- (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744).
-- SEAT: the notified body. In this part the text addresses notified bodies in one place that puts something on them: the exit report and the written proof that a national competent authority
-- provides for a sandbox "shall be taken positively into account by market surveillance authorities and notified bodies" (Article 57(7), second subparagraph, last sentence).
-- Article 58(2)(f) names notified bodies only as actors the sandboxes are to involve, and Article 65(6) names the notified bodies as the subject of one sub-group of the Board; neither puts a duty or a right on a notified body.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question calls one layer-1 function.
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs: a yes/no, a date, each with an @desc. The date asked comes first. `General` applies from 2 August 2026.
-- Commencement is IN for this Regulation (assumed, not ruled). The text is the Publications Office consolidation of 27.7.2026, a rendering with no legal effect.

§ `Under Article 57: the group General`

-- The applicability question for the provision group `General` that Article 57 opens in this part's range: it asks only the date, and passes the core's constants for the route, the placement date and the change.
@export Under Article 57, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `General` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)


§ `Under Article 57(7): the exit report and the written proof of a sandbox`

-- Article 57(7), second subparagraph, last sentence: "the exit reports and the written proof provided by the national competent authority shall be taken positively into account by market surveillance authorities and notified bodies, with a view to accelerating conformity assessment procedures to a reasonable extent".
@export Under Article 57, as a notified body, have I taken the exit report and the written proof of the AI regulatory sandbox positively into account, with a view to accelerating the conformity assessment procedure to a reasonable extent?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the exit report or the written proof was provided by the national competent authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the exit report, or the written proof, provided by the national competent authority?
      `the notified body takes the exit report and the written proof positively into account with a view to accelerating conformity assessment procedures to a reasonable extent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you taken the exit report and the written proof positively into account, with a view to accelerating the conformity assessment procedure to a reasonable extent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 57, as a notified body, have I taken the exit report and the written proof of the AI regulatory sandbox positively into account, with a view to accelerating the conformity assessment procedure to a reasonable extent` IS
    `Art 57(7) the notified body has taken the exit report and the written proof positively into account` `the date asked` `the exit report or the written proof was provided by the national competent authority` `the notified body takes the exit report and the written proof positively into account with a view to accelerating conformity assessment procedures to a reasonable extent`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat notified from part P8 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- P8 seat layer: a notified body: the confidentiality it owes (Article 78), the tests the Commission may entrust to it (Article 75(1e)) and the provider's duty to cooperate with it (Article 73(6)).
-- SEAT: a notified body
--
-- Nothing here is new law: each question calls the layer-1 function of Articles 72 to 79 (P8-art72 to P8-art79) that answers it, and the keel
-- (aia-definitions, aia-timeline, aia-core) for the role facts and the dates. Every question takes plain inputs: a yes/no, a date, a number or
-- one of the keel's own choices, each with an @desc worded for the person asking. A question answers JUST value, or NOTHING where the text does
-- not decide it (the Regulation does not apply yet on the date asked, or the text is silent); a JUST FALSE is a "no" the text itself gives.
-- Questions are grouped by Article in the order of the text; the role question and the applicability questions come first.


§ `The role the person asking holds`

-- The role, worked out by the keel's definition; the other questions of this seat assume it.
@export Under Article 73, as a notified body, am I a notified body within the meaning of Article 3(22)?
GIVEN `the body is a conformity assessment body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a conformity assessment body?
      `it is notified in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you notified in accordance with this Regulation?
      `it is notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or is no other such legislation relevant?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 73, as a notified body, am I a notified body within the meaning of Article 3(22)` IS
    `Art 3(22) the body is a notified body` `the body is a conformity assessment body` `it is notified in accordance with this Regulation` `it is notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant`

§ `Which provisions apply on the date asked`

-- Calls the gate helper of P8-gate, which passes the group to the keel's `Art 113 the provision group applies`.
@export Under Article 72, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 72, as a notified body, does General apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Arts 72 to 79 the group General applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)

-- Calls the gate helper of P8-gate, which passes the group to the keel's `Art 113 the provision group applies`.
@export Under Article 78, as a notified body, does Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 78, as a notified body, does Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)

§ `Article 73: Reporting of serious incidents`
-- Arises only after a serious incident of a high-risk AI system placed on the Union market.

-- Calls `Art 73(6) second subparagraph the provider has met the duty to cooperate with the competent authorities and, where relevant, the notified body concerned`.
@export Under Article 73(6), as a notified body, has the provider met its duty to cooperate with me as the notified body concerned during the investigations?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system, which is high-risk under Article 6(1), related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I? Answer no if it is not, or if you do not know.
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under the Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation? This does not change the answer to this question; Article 2(2) uses it for other Articles. Answer no if you do not know.
      `the provider cooperates with the competent authorities during the investigations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the provider cooperates with the competent authorities during the investigations?
      `the notified body concerned is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notified body concerned is relevant?
      `the provider cooperates with the notified body concerned during the investigations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the provider cooperates with the notified body concerned during the investigations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 73(6), as a notified body, has the provider met its duty to cooperate with me as the notified body concerned during the investigations` IS
    `Art 73(6) second subparagraph the provider has met the duty to cooperate with the competent authorities and, where relevant, the notified body concerned` `the date asked` `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `the provider cooperates with the competent authorities during the investigations` `the notified body concerned is relevant` `the provider cooperates with the notified body concerned during the investigations`

§ `Article 75: Market surveillance and control of AI systems and mutual assistance`
-- Arises only if the AI Office is competent for the AI system (Article 75(1)), or the Commission arranges a third-party conformity assessment (Article 75(1e)).

-- Calls `Art 75(1e) third sentence the Commission must entrust the performance of the tests or assessments to notified bodies, which act on behalf of the Commission`.
@export Under Article 75(1e), as a notified body, must the Commission entrust the performance of the tests or assessments to notified bodies, which act on its behalf?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the AI Office is responsible for the tests and assessments under this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the AI Office is responsible for the tests and assessments under this paragraph?
      `the notified body is designated in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the notified body is designated in accordance with this Regulation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 75(1e), as a notified body, must the Commission entrust the performance of the tests or assessments to notified bodies, which act on its behalf` IS
    `Art 75(1e) third sentence the Commission must entrust the performance of the tests or assessments to notified bodies, which act on behalf of the Commission` `the date asked` `the AI Office is responsible for the tests and assessments under this paragraph` `the notified body is designated in accordance with this Regulation`

-- Calls `Art 75(1e) fourth sentence the Commission may withdraw the delegation with immediate effect`.
@export Under Article 75(1e), as a notified body, may the Commission withdraw the delegation with immediate effect?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `a notified body to which the Commission has delegated tasks under this paragraph does not perform those tasks adequately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a notified body to which the Commission has delegated tasks under this paragraph does not perform those tasks adequately?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 75(1e), as a notified body, may the Commission withdraw the delegation with immediate effect` IS
    `Art 75(1e) fourth sentence the Commission may withdraw the delegation with immediate effect` `the date asked` `a notified body to which the Commission has delegated tasks under this paragraph does not perform those tasks adequately`

§ `Article 78: Confidentiality`
-- Arises only for the confidentiality of information obtained in the application of the Regulation; the provider question arises only if the provider is a law enforcement, immigration or asylum authority.

-- Calls `Art 78(1) the party must respect the confidentiality of the information and data obtained in carrying out its tasks and activities`.
@export Under Article 78(1), as a notified body, must I respect the confidentiality of the information and data I obtain in carrying out my tasks and activities?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the party is the Commission, a market surveillance authority, a notified body or any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party is the Commission, a market surveillance authority, a notified body or any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation?
      `the party has obtained information and data in carrying out its tasks and activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party has obtained information and data in carrying out its tasks and activities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 78(1), as a notified body, must I respect the confidentiality of the information and data I obtain in carrying out my tasks and activities` IS
    `Art 78(1) the party must respect the confidentiality of the information and data obtained in carrying out its tasks and activities` `the date asked` `the party is the Commission, a market surveillance authority, a notified body or any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation` `the party has obtained information and data in carrying out its tasks and activities`

-- Calls `Art 78(1) the confidentiality that the party respects is to protect the interest`.
@export Under Article 78(1), as a notified body, is the confidentiality that I respect to protect the interest in question?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the interest` IS A `Art 78(1) interest that the confidentiality protects` @desc Which of these applies to the interest? Choose one of: Art 78(1)(a) the intellectual property rights and confidential business information or trade secrets of a natural or legal person, including source code; Art 78(1)(b) the effective implementation of this Regulation, in particular for the purposes of inspections, investigations or audits; Art 78(1)(c) public and national security interests; Art 78(1)(d) the conduct of criminal or administrative proceedings; Art 78(1)(e) information classified pursuant to Union or national law; Art 78(1) any other interest that the list does not name.
      `the case is one referred to in Article 5 of Directive (EU) 2016/943` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the case is one referred to in Article 5 of Directive (EU) 2016/943?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 78(1), as a notified body, is the confidentiality that I respect to protect the interest in question` IS
    `Art 78(1) the confidentiality that the party respects is to protect the interest` `the date asked` `the interest` `the case is one referred to in Article 5 of Directive (EU) 2016/943`

-- Calls `Art 78(4) paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 do not affect the rights or obligations of the Commission, the Member States and their relevant authorities, and of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings`.
@export Under Article 78(4), as a notified body, do paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 not affect my rights or obligations regarding the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the matter is a right or obligation of the Commission, Member States and their relevant authorities, or of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings, including in the context of cross-border cooperation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the matter is a right or obligation of the Commission, Member States and their relevant authorities, or of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings, including in the context of cross-border cooperation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 78(4), as a notified body, do paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 not affect my rights or obligations regarding the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings` IS
    `Art 78(4) paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 do not affect the rights or obligations of the Commission, the Member States and their relevant authorities, and of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings` `the date asked` `the matter is a right or obligation of the Commission, Member States and their relevant authorities, or of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings, including in the context of cross-border cooperation`

-- ====================================================================================================
-- seat questions of seat notified from part P9 (merged; unchanged text follows)
-- ====================================================================================================
-- Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 -- P9 -- THE SEAT LAYER, Articles 80 to 112.
--
-- SEAT: a notified body.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions this person would ask
-- about the Articles of P9 (market surveillance of AI systems, complaints and explanations, enforcement of the rules on
-- general-purpose AI models, codes of conduct and guidelines, penalties, and the final provisions). Nothing here is new law:
-- each question calls one layer-1 function and builds the record that function expects (the `AI system`) in a WHERE from
-- the answers. The rules a question calls are the ones that carry the quotes, the glosses and the NOTHING/FALSE branches.
-- Every question except the role question takes `the date asked`, so the answer is the Regulation as it stood or will stand on that date; a question
-- about an AI system also takes the AI system's route, the date it was placed on the market and whether its design has been
-- significantly changed, for Article 111(2). A group that is not yet in application answers NOTHING, never JUST FALSE.
-- The applicability question of each group the seat meets is the first question of its group of Articles.
-- The seat's own role is asked once, in the role question, which calls the keel's definition and has no date (a definition
-- of Article 3 is not asked on a date here); the other questions assume it.
-- Powers and duties of an official (the Commission, the AI Office, a market surveillance authority, the European Data
-- Protection Supervisor, a Member State) appear only as what they mean to this seat.
§ `Under Article 99: the applicability question for the group Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78`

@ref Art 113
@export Under Article 99, as a notified body, does Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 apply on the date asked?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 99, as a notified body, does Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78 apply on the date asked` IS
    JUST (`Art 113 the provision group applies` `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78` `the date asked` `the route to pass when no AI system is in question` `the date to pass when no AI system is in question` FALSE)

§ `The seat's role: Article 3(22)`

@ref Art 3
@export Under Article 99, as a notified body, am I a notified body within the meaning of Article 3(22)?
GIVEN `the body is a conformity assessment body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a conformity assessment body, that is, a body that performs third-party conformity assessment activities, including testing, certification and inspection?
      `it is notified in accordance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it notified in accordance with this Regulation?
      `it is notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation? Answer yes also if no other such legislation is relevant.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 99, as a notified body, am I a notified body within the meaning of Article 3(22)` IS
    JUST (`Art 3(22) the body is a notified body` `the body is a conformity assessment body` `it is notified in accordance with this Regulation` `it is notified in accordance with other relevant Union harmonisation legislation, or no other such legislation is relevant`)

§ `Under Article 99(4)(f)`

@ref Art 99(4)(f)
@export Under Article 99(4)(f), as a notified body, is my non-compliance with the requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34 subject to administrative fines?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the route by which the AI system is high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk` @desc Is the AI system high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I, because of Article 6(2) with Annex III, or neither?
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the AI system first placed on the market or put into service in the Union? If that has not happened yet, give the date you expect.
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Since the date from which Chapter III of the Regulation applies to your AI system, has its design been significantly changed? Answer no if you do not know of a significant change.
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the AI system related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I to the Regulation? Answer no if you do not know. This matters only if the AI system is high-risk because of Article 6(1) with Annex I.
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation? Answer no if you do not know. It decides nothing about the Articles asked here (it matters only to Articles 57, 58 and 59), but the same question is asked of every provision that Article 2(2) can cut off.
      `the non-compliance or the supply is established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the non-compliance (or the supply of the information) been established?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Article 99(4)(f), as a notified body, is my non-compliance with the requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34 subject to administrative fines` IS
    `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` `Art 99(4)(f) non-compliance with the requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34` `the non-compliance or the supply is established`
    WHERE
        `the AI system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
            `date placed on the market or put into service` IS `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service`
            `route` IS `the route by which the AI system is high-risk`
            `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`

@ref Art 99(4)(f)
@export Under Article 99(4)(f), as a notified body, what is the ceiling of the administrative fine for my non-compliance with the requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34?
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you want the answer? Give today's date for the Regulation as it stands today, or an earlier or later date for the Regulation as it stood or will stand then.
      `the offender is an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offender an undertaking?
      `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year, in euros?
      `the offender is an SME, including a start-up` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offender a small or medium-sized enterprise, including a start-up?
      `the offender is an SMC` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offender a small mid-cap enterprise (SMC)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Article 99(4)(f), as a notified body, what is the ceiling of the administrative fine for my non-compliance with the requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34` IS
    `Art 99 the ceiling of the administrative fine` `the date asked` `Art 99(4)(f) non-compliance with the requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34` `the offender is an undertaking` `the total worldwide annual turnover of the offender for the preceding financial year in euros` `the offender is an SME, including a start-up` `the offender is an SMC`
